  "passage": "A small rain shelter stood beside the road near school. It was old, and only three people could stand under it comfortably.\nDuring a storm, many students crowded there. A tall student noticed that younger students were getting wet at the edge. He stepped into the rain and gave them space.\nThe next day, someone had written on the shelter wall: \"Thank you to the boy who stood in the rain.\"\nNo name was written, but many students knew who it was.\nThe school later asked the city to build a larger shelter. Still, people remembered the small one because it had shown a quiet kind of kindness: making room for others even when it costs comfort.",
